---
layout: base.njk
pagination:
  data: collections.etcPage
  size: 1
  alias: etcPage
  addAllPagesToCollections: false
permalink: /etc/
title: etc
description: Everything else I write about, busiest first.
---
{#- The etc tab's page (2026-11-03): every group not in `tabs:`, each with
    its subjects under it, ranked by frecency (eleventy.config.js → frecency:
    recent writing weighs most, an essay three times a section). The tab
    links here, so nothing in etc is ever out of reach, however many groups
    it holds — the views row shows the busiest few, this shows all of them
    (Hat: "I don't want to exceed the limit and forget for three months and
    then a bunch of things aren't accessible"). A one-subject group's name
    goes straight to that subject's page; a bigger one's to its group page.

    Sort, in CSS, the shelf's way: each row carries its rank on every axis
    (etcRanks), and the checked radio picks which one `order` reads. DOM
    order is the score order, so the default needs no rule.

    A group with a shelf lists only the subjects it has writing on, and
    points the rest at its shelf: movies has 43 films and writing on two, and
    a list of 41 "nothing yet" rows buried every other group. A group with
    no shelf lists every subject, since nowhere else does. -#}
{%- set groups = collections.etcGroups %}
<article class="tag etc-page">
  <header class="tag-head group-head">
    <h1><span class="mico m-etc" aria-hidden="true"></span>etc</h1>
    <p class="tag-desc">{{ description }}</p>
  </header>
  <div class="etc-sorter">
    {% if groups | length > 1 %}
    <fieldset class="shelf-sort">
      <legend>sort</legend>
      <input type="radio" name="etc-sort" id="etc-score" checked>
      <label for="etc-score">busiest</label>
      <input type="radio" name="etc-sort" id="etc-recent">
      <label for="etc-recent">most recent</label>
      <input type="radio" name="etc-sort" id="etc-written">
      <label for="etc-written">most written</label>
    </fieldset>
    {% endif %}
    <ol class="etc-groups">
      {% for g in groups %}
      <li class="etc-group" style="--o-score:{{ g.oScore }};--o-recent:{{ g.oRecent }};--o-written:{{ g.oWritten }}">
        <h2 class="etc-group-head"><a href="{{ g.homeUrl }}">{% if g.hasIcon %}<span class="mico m-{{ g.id }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>{% endif %}{{ g.label }}</a></h2>
        {% if g.description %}<p class="tag-desc">{{ g.description }}</p>{% endif %}
        {#- A marginalia group's heading is its page; its one subject has no
            page of its own to list (2026-11-13). -#}
        {% if g.layout != "marginalia" %}
        <ul class="essay-list etc-subjects">
          {%- set listed = (g.subjects | selectattr("written") | list) if g.hasShelf else g.subjects %}
          {% for s in listed %}
          <li style="--o-score:{{ s.oScore }};--o-recent:{{ s.oRecent }};--o-written:{{ s.oWritten }}">
            <span class="sky" style="background-image:url({{ s.chipUrl }})" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <a href="/s/{{ s.slug }}/">{{ s.title }}</a>
            <span class="archive-note">{% if s.lastWrote %}{{ s.written }} {% if s.written == 1 %}entry{% else %}entries{% endif %} · last {{ s.lastWrote | shortDate }}{% else %}nothing yet{% endif %}</span>
          </li>
          {% endfor %}
          {%- set rest = (g.subjects | length) - (listed | length) %}
          {% if rest > 0 %}
          <li class="etc-more"><a href="{{ g.urls.shelf }}">{{ rest }} more on the shelf →</a></li>
          {% endif %}
        </ul>
        {% endif %}
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
</article>
